.TH LLAMA-RUNNER 1 "2026-11-07" "llama-runner 1.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
llama-runner \- launch llama-server and wire it to Claude Code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llama-runner
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B llama-runner
starts a local \fBllama-server\fR with a GGUF model and, by default, launches
Claude Code wired to that server through \fBANTHROPIC_*\fR environment
variables. When Claude Code exits, the server is stopped.
.PP
With \fB-server\fR only llama-server is started. With \fB-doctor\fR a
read-only report of resolved paths, version, and the final llama-server
command line is printed without spawning any processes. With \fB-update\fR
llama.cpp is rebuilt and installed, then the program exits.
.PP
In hybrid mode (\fB-openai\fR + \fB-model-openai\fR + key or \fB-key none\fR)
a local proxy routes Claude Code requests between the local llama-server and
the external OpenAI-compatible provider. The local route is a verbatim
passthrough to \fB/v1/messages\fR (native Anthropic API).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-model \fIpath\fR
Path to the GGUF model. Default: \fI~/GGUF/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf\fR.
.TP
.B \-bin \fIpath\fR
Path to llama-server. Default: \fI~/.local/bin/llama-server\fR.
.TP
.B \-alias \fIname\fR
Model alias used for llama-server \-\-alias and \fBANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL\fR.
When unset, derived from the model file name, then from the config file or
profile, then defaults to \fBlocal\fR.
.TP
.B \-server
Start llama-server only, without Claude Code.
.TP
.B \-doctor
Print resolved paths, version, and the final llama-server command; do not
spawn any processes.
.TP
.B \-update
Update llama.cpp (git pull --ff-only, cmake configure/build/install) and exit.
.TP
.B \-download \fI<dir><url>\fR
Download a GGUF model (single file or Hugging Face shard set) before launch.
Passing any shard of a sharded model downloads the whole set and uses shard 1.
.TP
.B \-c, \-b, \-ub \fIn\fR
Context / batch / micro-batch sizes passed to llama-server.
.TP
.B \-ngl \fIn\fR
Number of layers offloaded to GPU.
.TP
.B \-chat-template \fIvalue\fR
\fBauto\fR, \fB""\fR (use the template embedded in the GGUF), or a path to a
Jinja template file.
.TP
.B \-openai \fIurl\fR, \-model-openai \fIname\fR, \-key \fIkey\fR
External OpenAI-compatible provider. \fB-key none\fR or \fB-key ""\fR means
the provider needs no authentication; the request then carries no
\fBAuthorization\fR header at all.
.TP
.B \-proxy-addr \fIhost:port\fR
Address of the local routing proxy. Default: \fI127.0.0.1:8082\fR.
.TP
.B \-proxy-token \fIvalue\fR
If set, the proxy rejects incoming requests without a matching
\fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR or \fBx-api-key\fR.
.TP
.B \-config \fIpath\fR
Configuration file. Default: \fI~/.config/llama-runner/config.json\fR.
\fB-config ""\fR disables reading the file.
.TP
.B \-p \fIname\fR
Profile from the config file.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the command before running it.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/llama-runner/config.json
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/llama-runner/credentials
Optional \fBKEY=VALUE\fR file for the external provider key
(\fBOPENAI_KEY\fR or \fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fR). Permissions \fB0600\fR recommended.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/llama-runner/llama-server.log
Default llama-server log file (rotated by size; see \fB-log-max-mb\fR and
\fB-log-keep\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/llama-runner/proxy.log
Proxy diagnostics when the server log is not enabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LLAMA_RUNNER_OPENAI_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY
External provider API key, used only when the external provider is actually
requested. The \fB-key\fR flag, if given, outranks both.
.TP
.B HF_TOKEN, HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN
Hugging Face access token, used by \fB-download\fR for gated repositories.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start llama-server and Claude Code with a project directory:
.B llama-runner -claude-dir ~/my-project
.TP
Start the server only on a different port:
.B llama-runner -server -port 9090
.TP
Hybrid mode with a proxy token:
.B llama-runner -openai https://api.example.com/v1 -key \$KEY -model-openai model-x -proxy-token \$TOKEN
.TP
Diagnostics without starting anything:
.B llama-runner -doctor
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR llama-server (1),
.BR claude (1),
.BR curl (1)
